{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during your stay. You came in with chest pain—can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started three days ago. It’s in the middle of my chest, like pressure, and goes to my back and sometimes my left jaw."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How long does it last? Does anything make it better or worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It comes and goes. This morning I took nitroglycerin and it went from a 10 to a 7. But it didn’t go away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You mentioned you had a stent placed three weeks ago?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, in the right coronary artery. My PCP said it was done, and I’ve been on aspirin and prasugrel since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check that. We’ve ruled out a heart attack—your troponins were normal and EKG didn’t show changes. But we want to make sure the stent is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had chest pain off and on for years. Thought it was anxiety, but this feels different."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:08:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also checking for other causes—like blood clots or aortic issues. Your CT scan was clear for those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. I’ve also been short of breath walking to the bathroom, which isn’t normal for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:10:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. You have a history of heart failure, but no current fluid overload. We’ll monitor that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I sleep on three pillows—always have. But no swelling in my legs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:13:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s chronic for you, so we’re not concerned about acute heart failure. We’ll do an echo to check heart function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:14:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And I’ve had nausea and loose stools the past day—could that be related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2145-08-20 16:15:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll check labs. Could be from stress, meds, or GI issues. We may involve GI if it continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your echo showed normal heart function—LVEF over 55%. No wall motion issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. So why the chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not sure yet. Since heart tests are normal, we’re considering other causes—like esophageal issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like acid reflux?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ve consulted GI. They suggest continuing your pantoprazole and adding TUMS for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on pantoprazole for a while. Should we increase it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2145-08-21 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re already on 40 mg twice daily—the max dose. We’ll stick with that and add TUMS as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2145-08-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning a heart cath tomorrow to check your stent. Even though tests are normal, we want to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2145-08-22 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? I’ve had radial access before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2145-08-22 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very routine. We’ll use the wrist again. Main risk is minor bleeding or bruising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2145-08-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my arm swelled last time—should I worry?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2145-08-22 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. If it swells, we’ll check with ultrasound to rule out clot or bleed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well during the cath. The stent in your RCA is open, no blockages. The other arteries look stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not from a blockage. But we did find elevated pressure in the left side of your heart—LVEDP was high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Does that mean heart failure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. You’re not retaining fluid or short of breath at rest. We’ll watch it and may add a diuretic if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. So what’s causing the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely esophageal—like GERD. The pain pattern fits, and heart causes are ruled out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I should keep taking the pantoprazole and TUMS?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2145-08-23 14:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And GI wants to see you in a week. They’ll discuss an endoscopy to look inside your esophagus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2145-08-24 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My right forearm is itchy and a little swollen where they did the cath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2145-08-24 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Looks like a mild reaction—probably hives. We’ll give you Benadryl and a steroid cream."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2145-08-24 11:02:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could it be a blood clot?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2145-08-24 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do an ultrasound to be sure. But it looks like a skin reaction, not a clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—the ultrasound showed no clot or bleed. Just a local reaction. It should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So am I ready to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your heart is stable, pain is manageable, and we’ve ruled out serious causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking all your meds—especially aspirin, prasugrel, and the pantoprazole. Use TUMS for chest discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your cardiologist soon. And GI in a week for the endoscopy. Call if chest pain worsens or you have swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my blood pressure? It’s been high in here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We kept your usual meds—amlodipine, losartan, carvedilol. They’re managing it. Keep monitoring at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:11:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes? My glucose was high this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stress can raise it. Keep taking metformin and glipizide. Check sugars and report any consistent highs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:14:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling down lately. Should I talk to someone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your sertraline and trazodone are continued. Please follow up with your psychiatrist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:16:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2145-08-25 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be out by noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2145-08-25 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Here’s your discharge summary. You’re going home with instructions to continue all meds and follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2145-08-25 12:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if my chest pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2145-08-25 12:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Try TUMS or nitroglycerin. If it doesn’t improve in 10 minutes or gets worse, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2145-08-25 12:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll call GI and cardiology to schedule visits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2145-08-25 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2145-08-20 15:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2145-08-25 17:39:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of coronary artery disease, hypertension, type 2 diabetes, hyperlipidemia, pseudotumor cerebri with a VP shunt, obstructive sleep apnea, depression, and obesity was admitted for substernal chest pain radiating to the back and jaw. Initial evaluation showed no acute coronary syndrome, with normal troponins and EKG. A cardiac catheterization revealed a patent stent in the right coronary artery and no high-grade stenosis, though elevated left ventricular end-diastolic pressure was noted without clinical heart failure. The chest pain was ultimately attributed to a likely esophageal etiology, such as GERD, and managed with pantoprazole and TUMS. GI follow-up was arranged for outpatient endoscopy. She also developed mild right forearm swelling post-cath, which resolved with conservative treatment and was confirmed as non-thrombotic on ultrasound. She remained stable, adherent to medications, and was discharged home with plans for cardiology and GI follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chest pain",
      "Hypertensive heart disease with heart failure",
      "Unspecified diastolic (congestive) heart failure",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary artery without angina pectoris",
      "Presence of coronary angioplasty implant and graft",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Presence of cerebrospinal fluid drainage device",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 39.0-39.9, adult",
      "Long term (current) use of antithrombotics/antiplatelets",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence"
    ]
  }
}
